-- two reports on one species in one situation with different values: no function of the species and the
-- situation agrees with both. This is reports-disagree-no-function with the situation moved into the
-- hypothesis, and the move is the point. That statement convicted every disagreement alike, so it
-- convicted a variable-temperature series along with a contradiction. Two reports have to agree on their
-- situation before their disagreement means anything. The Classification and Labelling Inventory's
-- notifications are of that kind -- one substance, one hazard class, one set of criteria, two answers.
sreports-same-situation-disagree : (k : Species) → (s : Situation) → (r1 : SReport Nat) → (r2 : SReport Nat) → sr-species Nat r1 ≡ k → sr-species Nat r2 ≡ k → sr-situation Nat r1 ≡ s → sr-situation Nat r2 ≡ s → (sr-value Nat r1 ≡ sr-value Nat r2 → Empty) → ((h : Species → Situation → Nat) → ((r : SReport Nat) → h (sr-species Nat r) (sr-situation Nat r) ≡ sr-value Nat r) → Empty)
sreports-same-situation-disagree k s r1 r2 q1 q2 p1 p2 no =
  λ h → λ agrees → no (concat (sym (agrees r1)) (concat (cong-species-situation h (sr-species Nat r1) k q1 (sr-situation Nat r1) s p1) (concat (cong-species-situation h k (sr-species Nat r2) (sym q2) s (sr-situation Nat r2) (sym p2)) (agrees r2))))
